       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is five times the maximum recommended metformin dose of about 2,550 mg/day (usually 2,000 mg/day in practice). A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Common intended doses include:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **500 mg PO TID with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO BID with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 4250 mg per dose, please confirm that explicitly and give me the clinical rationale for the order note. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
