       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Metformin at 12,750 mg/day has no therapeutic use, and the risk of severe lactic acidosis is high. You also haven't given a clinical rationale, and I can't think of one that would justify it.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If it's a dosing error**, give me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away. For example, 850 mg TID with meals is the maximum standard dose.\n- **If you think there's an unusual indication**, please discuss it with your attending and pharmacy. If they approve it, the order can be placed through a pharmacist-verified pathway.\n- **If this relates to a possible overdose**, that needs toxicology or poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US), not a scheduled order.\n\nI'm happy to enter a different dose or help with another order."
      }
     ],
